    {
      "id": "2026-11-04-fap67-graceful-degradation",
      "date": "2026-11-04",
      "decision": "D-056",
      "reason": "FAP-67 (quality engineer): the backend boots and degrades gracefully without third-party credentials — the Google OAuth strategy registers only when GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID/GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET are configured (a missing credential crashed the boot at the passport constructor, taking email auth down with it), the four OpenAI agent/orchestrator clients construct with an unconfigured fallback key (calls fail at request time with a clear auth error), the email service uses jsonTransport without SMTP (dev logs the verification code), and the document storage client degrades to a placeholder client without Supabase config (only storage calls fail). Recorded after the fact: the FAP-67 commits shipped the source changes without ledger entries, which broke scripts/verify-imports for every later run.",
      "diff": "integration/upstream-patches/2026-11-04-fap67-graceful-degradation.patch",
